  "rationale": "A fixed-horizon market return must include the price change from the last causally observed price at or before the window boundary to the first later trade inside the window. The frozen implementation instead began at the first in-window trade, suppressing the first move and making the measured horizon depend on trade arrival intensity. Flow counts and notionals remain strictly in-window. Separately, the frozen promotion gate required dependence-aware confidence only for log-loss improvement while accepting Brier improvement from a point estimate. The corrected gate requires an independently seeded stationary-bootstrap upper bound below zero for both strictly proper scores. No outcome, threshold, candidate family, economic rule, or authority was used or relaxed.",
